updates={
'PROJECT.md':'The default entry is now River history: 2015–2024 daily ERA5/GloFAS estimates (3,653 days), a year selector, synchronized daily flow visualization and 120-month comparison grid. The resource map retains the nine-day event-detail window. The search circle is removed entirely. Actual flood extent/depth visualization remains pending observed footprints or validated hydraulic outputs.',
'DESIGN.md':'The rejected search circle is removed, including its layer toggle and legend. The entry screen is River history: ten-year month tiles, a fixed-scale annual hydrograph, click/scrub date selection, replay/pause, previous-day flow change and a discharge column. The column encodes discharge, not water height. A separate explicit gap panel explains that mapped flood spread is unavailable. The old nine-day resource workspace remains accessible under Explore.',
'SPEC.md':'RiverHistory consumes flow-history.json and rain-history.json (2015-01-01–2024-12-31). Dates join by calendar label while keeping UTC/IST distinctions explicit; null rainfall remains null. Graph scale and monthly peak colors are fixed to the full ten-year discharge maximum, not flood-risk thresholds. Monthly tiles jump to the observed-in-this-model maximum date; replay advances daily or weekly and pauses explicitly. CSV includes every daily row. No water depth or flood extent is inferred.',
'DECISION.md':'User rejected the static resource emphasis, short time window and confusing blue circle. Removed the circle, made ten-year visual history the default, preserved resource review as a secondary workspace. Do not replace the circle with invented inundation geometry. Actual rising/spreading flood visualization is an outstanding separate deliverable requiring observed satellite footprints or validated hydraulic results.',
'MISTAKE.md':'A resource-search circle looked like a hazard footprint even with a label. Removed it rather than trying to explain it better. A nine-day detail window is not adequate long-term environmental context; added ten complete years. Visualizing discharge is useful but does not fulfill the still-open requirement to show which land floods.',
'TASKS.md':'River history added: 2015–2024, 3,653 daily records, 120 monthly peak tiles, synchronized replay and CSV export. Search circle removed. Nine history-browser checks and the original thirteen workflow checks pass against the production preview. Actual spatial flood spread remains unimplemented, not represented by the flow column.',
'docs/DATA.md':'Added flow-history.json and rain-history.json, requested 2015-01-01–2024-12-31 at the same respective grid cells. Each contains 3,653 daily timestamps, downloaded 4 November 2026. Queries, SHA-256 fingerprints, returned coordinates, model, units and limitations are in public/data/manifest.json. Flow is daily GloFAS m³/s (UTC); rainfall is daily ERA5 precipitation sum in mm (IST). Same licensing/representativeness limits as the original snapshots. No flooded-area measurements were obtained.',
'docs/DELIVERY.md':'New default River history passes nine browser checks in tests/history-check.mjs: ten-year data/120 tiles, synchronized flow rise, leap years, peak selection, replay/pause, full export, circle removal, 360px layout and no unhandled errors. Existing thirteen workflow checks also pass with explicit Explore navigation. Production build passes. Evidence: artifacts/history-report.json; artifacts/history-desktop.png; artifacts/history-mobile.png; artifacts/history-video. No physical-phone or inundation validation claim. The requested actual mapped flood-rise/spread visualization is still outstanding.',
'README.md':'Start on River history to explore 2015–2024 (3,653 daily records). Pick a year, click a monthly peak tile or scrub/play the daily graph. Export the complete ten-year CSV. Explore opens the existing resource-review workspace. Run `node tests/history-check.mjs` against preview port 4173 for the new visual journey. The blue search circle has been removed; no actual flood extent or water depth is currently displayed.'}
for name,text in updates.items():
 p=Path(name);s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s+='\n\n## Visual history revision — 4 November 2026\n\n'+text+'\n';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
